                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^N
            \-models” one refers to (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"}> topological
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            — often (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+strings"}> topological
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theories"} string theories
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            is 2-dimensional — with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^N
            such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^1
          %blockquote
            %p
              %a{:href => "#NakayamaFunckeJansenKaoKühn22"}> NFJKK22
              \: “The
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CP
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CP(N-1)
              models in 1+1 dimensions share many properties with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              in 3+1 dimensions, among them
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+freedom"} asymptotic freedom
              = succeed "," do
